---
const commands = `sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install --yes --no-install-recommends ca-certificates git
git clone https://github.com/melloa-project/melloa.git
cd melloa
sudo infra/server/bootstrap-debian.sh --source "$PWD" --self-change-tools

cd ..
git clone https://github.com/melloa-project/melloa-guardian.git
cd melloa-guardian
make preview-state
cd ../melloa

sudo infra/server/first-install.sh --source "$PWD"`;
---

<section class="melloa-command-spine" aria-labelledby="melloa-command-spine-title">
  <div class="melloa-command-copy">
    <p class="melloa-eyebrow">First server path</p>
    <h2 id="melloa-command-spine-title">
      Clone it, pair Telegram, talk to Melli, then improve the system from inside the system.
    </h2>
    <p>
      Start hosted-provider-first. No local GPU is expected for the first deployment. The first
      proof is a real Telegram conversation followed by one bounded owner-approved self-change.
    </p>
  </div>
  <pre aria-label="Melloa first server command spine"><code>{commands}</code></pre>
</section>
